Optional future snapshot licences - no present grant

Daniel may choose, at his sole discretion and subject to existing obligations,
to grant a separate written, non-exclusive licence to a named business, including
a future AI agency. The grant must identify the covered material in one or more
repositories by commit, archive hash or other fixed snapshot and state the
permitted use. This notice grants no such licence, contractual option, or right
to demand a licence.

A separate grant can authorize one baseline handoff into the recipient's own
repositories, followed by continuing use, copying, backups, deployment,
modification and independent development within its agreed business scope. It
can expressly permit running client services and charging for those services.
These activities require the actual grant; this policy is not their permission.

"One-time" describes the identified baseline handoff, not a single execution or
a ban on copies needed for the licensed work. It creates no entitlement to later
versions, future repositories, updates, support, synchronization or further
source deliveries. The separate grant determines its duration and other terms.

Permission to operate client services does not itself authorize selling or
distributing the covered source or a starter kit containing it, sublicensing or
transferring the licensed material, or a founder taking it into an unrelated
business. Those activities, including where protected baseline material remains
in a modified version, require Daniel's separate written authorization, subject
to the existing rights and legal exceptions preserved above.

Importing the baseline into another repository and later divergence do not
